<%# views/privacy.ejs
    The privacy notice. Everyone must agree to it when they register.
    PLACEHOLDER TEXT: Koulla is writing the final wording. To update it,
    replace the text between the header and footer lines below. The three
    topics come from PRD section 4.1: data safety, how profile information
    is shown to other users, and consent to be contacted. %>
<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Privacy notice' }) %>

<h1>Privacy notice</h1>

<p class="notice">
  Draft wording. This notice is still being written and may change.
</p>

<p class="lead">
  What Bootcamp Connect stores about you, who can see it, and what you are
  agreeing to when you register.
</p>

<h2>What we store and how we keep it safe</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    Your name, email address, course, and the profile details you choose to
    add (what you are looking for, skills, interests, bio, business idea and
    photo).
  </li>
  <li>
    Your password is stored in a scrambled form. Nobody can read it, not
    even the people who run the app.
  </li>
  <li>The date you agreed to this notice.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What other users can see</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    Other logged-in students can see your name, course and profile details.
  </li>
  <li>Your email address is never shown on your profile.</li>
  <li>
    Messages can be read only by you and the person you are talking to.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Being contacted</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    By registering, you agree that other students on the bootcamp can send
    you a connection request.
  </li>
  <li>
    Nobody can message you until you have accepted their request. You can
    decline any request.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<ul>
  <li>You can change your profile at any time.</li>
  <li>
    You can delete your account. This removes your profile, your requests
    and your conversations.
  </li>
</ul>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
